 yeah you know we went through a little  short-term pain here and yeah it stirred  up some things and yeah we'd rather that  not happen but if it makes everybody  focused and motivated and determined to  be as good as they can be in 2019 that's  a good thing right chris yeah no i mean  it is and sometimes things like these  are like this can you know again bring a  locker room together and especially  maybe even aaron rodgers reassess how he  wants to lead going forward or whatever  it may be uh yeah i do think these  things can be positive listen i'm glad  that mark murphy addressed the situation  a little bit uh because you know i  didn't want to hear about you today  because you were going to come in with  all your conspiracy theories talking  about oh the packers haven't made a  statement and this looks real fishy and  rogers must be guilty of everything so  i'm glad he got that out again i think  they were letting this die down a little  bit mark murphy didn't want to make this  the biggest thing going on in the nfl  the first day back for otas or off  season workouts or whatever it may be  but again it's a new time there it's a  new culture the bad news and the bad  laundry is gone and they're trying to  move on from that and become more  positive and a new team here going into  2019  but you do have to admit that before  mark murphy speaks if there's a vacuum  if there's nothing from the packers in  response to an article that aaron  rodgers had come out and called a smear  attack and passionately pushed back  against the likes of jeremiah finley and  greg jennings and and seems to take  issue with everything in there and he is  clearly upset about it and and if he  truly believes that it's falsehoods that  they're embellished by the reporter to  boost his career and the team has said  nothing at all at a certain point that  does become a problem and i hey i i  could see aaron rodgers look at what  mark murphy said yesterday and say man  you really didn't come out against this  thing the way that i would have  preferred you're kind of laughing it off  as hey it's going to make us better in  2019 so yeah again when you're dealing  with somebody who has that reputation a  well-earned reputation of being  ultra-sensitive you have to  strategically think about everything you  say  and i would guess that if he would admit  it aaron rodgers ultimately not happy  with the way the packers have responded  to this report that he feels so  passionately about yeah well again i  don't think that the the green bay  packers wanted to fan the flames of this  story to start out the week on monday  and tuesday and just give it more juice  i think they were doing their best to  let it die down and i'll really go back  to something you've said over the week  that i think also plays into this this  you know situation you've talked about  you know no ownership factor there in  green bay  it's not in green bay's dna in their  history at least in my observations of  them having these type of moments you  know i mean the moments i'm not saying  the little dysfunction between rogers  and mccarthy i mean the moments of where  there's a head of the organization who  comes out and makes you know state of  the union type addresses on the team  regularly you know that with the owner  and a team like mr craft or jerry jones  and the cowboys they're always at times  going to get up there in front of the  microphones and give you the state of  the union what's going on with the team  and tell you their thoughts and i think  because of lack of ownership there in  green bay a different structure you  don't get that as much and maybe they're  a little slow to react to things like  this as well  well i i just think that their  their position early on was keep their  head low keep their mouth shut and let  it just go away but but there was a  disconnect between that strategy  and aaron rodgers strategy which was go  on espn radio and milwaukee and tear  this thing apart and basically if the  team's not going to do it then i guess i  have to do it i'm just trying to read  this from the perspective of how does  aaron rodgers feel about how the packers  have handled it and mark murphy finally  has spoken but i think it's fair to  wonder given everything we know about  aaron rodgers whether or not he's upset  at some level that they didn't address  it more quickly and that they didn't  attack it more aggressively more pft  live coming at you right after this  [Music]  hi i'm mike tarico and thanks for  watching make sure to hit subscribe for  the latest news and highlights from nbc  sports

